WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:07.640
SCP-1504 is an otherwise normal man who seems
to be invulnerable to all forms of harm and

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.480
is held in a standard human containment cell.

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:15.500
He knows his name is Joe, but does not seem
to be able to recall his last name, which

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.160
has led to him being given the nickname “Joe
Schmo”..

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:24.370
He was brought to a nearby SCP containment
site without incident to be interviewed and

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:25.370
studied.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:30.320
At first glance, it seems like it is one of
the least interesting entities in SCP containment,

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:35.570
but this seemingly uninteresting man turned
out to be a far more complicated case than

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:38.050
anyone at the Foundation expected.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.680
Dr. Loyd was not anticipating a difficult
interview when he stepped into the containment

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.140
cell to speak with SCP-1504.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:51.770
The mystery man was cooperative, answering
questions, although there were some abnormalities.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:57.390
Not only did this man not know his own last
name, but he didn’t know when he was born.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.070
As the interview went on, Dr. Loyd suffered
a spontaneous nosebleed and had to briefly

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.200
leave the room.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:09.450
Dr. Loyd returned and the interview went smoothly
- until he asked 1504 about the origin of

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.520
his invulnerability.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:16.140
The subject began crying and refused to talk
about it, and was released to his room.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.240
That’s where the trouble began.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:23.280
Dr. Loyd normally ran a rather calm site,
with high-tech security systems that were

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.670
effective at containing the entities inside.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.240
As long as the technology worked, the staff
was in no danger - and it was designed to

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.640
be foolproof.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.369
Or so they thought.

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:36.900
The technical hiccups began slowly.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.240
Doors would open when they weren’t supposed
to, but the resulting breaches were quickly

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.240
contained.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.549
These new issues were worrying, but as long
as they stayed manageable, the staff could

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:49.100
keep everything under control.

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.770
But of course, things didn’t stay manageable.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:56.750
The site had one dangerous keter entity on
hand that breached containment.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:02:00.869
When it broke out, the staff who specialized
in re-containing anomalies were alerted but

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:02.800
only about half responded.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.119
The other missing half were all dead.

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:10.239
The remaining staff barely survived and managed
to contain the Keter, but their troubles were

00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:11.790
only beginning.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.830
Requests for more staff went ignored.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:19.010
Supply drops didn’t arrive, and the staff
was quickly beginning to run out of the basics.

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:23.260
The deaths on site weren’t acknowledged
by the Foundation - or even many of the people

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.420
on site.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.219
It was as if they had never happened.

00:02:27.219 --> 00:02:31.700
Things were going from bad to worse - and
the true horrors lay ahead.

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.829
One day all the doors at the site suddenly
opened at once, and the staff was quickly

00:02:35.829 --> 00:02:39.420
overwhelmed by the freed and enraged entities.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:44.909
Most died, and the surviving ones scattered,
seemingly unconcerned with finding any other

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:45.909
survivors.

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:49.859
The only one who seemed aware of what was
happening was Darryl Loyd, and he knew there

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:52.639
was no way to contain this breach.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:56.200
His time was running out, and there was only
one thing left to do.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.099
He wrote everything that had happened down
in a document and sealed it in the indestructible

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:02.099
vault.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.099
The document opened with a chilling sentence.

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:06.680
“We didn’t know his true anomaly.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.090
We didn’t know what he could really do.”

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:14.769
Then, Dr. Loyd activated the fail-safe that
every SCP site has - an on-site nuke that

00:03:14.769 --> 00:03:18.930
can be triggered in the event of a breach
that would endanger the outside world.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:23.569
The badly injured Dr. Loyd perished in the
blast, along with every surviving staff member

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:26.459
and many of the escaped entities at the site.

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:30.879
When Foundation staff dug through the rubble,
they found the document - although it was

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:35.480
badly damaged and parts were unreadable due
to blood stains having been smeared across

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:36.480
it.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.359
Most of the anomalies kept at the site were
accounted for, but one entity was neither

00:03:40.359 --> 00:03:43.180
confirmed killed or recaptured.

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.439
So where was Joe Schmo?

00:03:45.439 --> 00:03:51.059
Not only was SCP-1504 not found on site, there
was very little record of him found on any

00:03:51.059 --> 00:03:53.599
electronic systems or archives.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:58.229
The only evidence found of this mysterious
man was the hand-written document left behind

00:03:58.229 --> 00:04:03.559
by the late Dr. Loyd, as well as the initial
interview that seemed to show absolutely nothing

00:04:03.559 --> 00:04:04.559
of note.

00:04:04.559 --> 00:04:09.870
But Dr. Loyd’s last words worried the staff,
and a missing entity is never to be taken

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:10.870
lightly.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:15.709
It was decided to run the interview footage
through multiple filters to rule out any perception-based

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:16.900
interference.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:21.600
What they discovered turned out to be one
of the biggest threats in the SCP Foundation’s

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:22.600
history.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:28.290
The interview started similarly, with Dr.
Loyd asking SCP-1504 what his name was.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.760
But things soon took a turn from the original
log.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:34.700
SCP-1504 was belligerent from the start.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.560
He snapped “I’m not going to tell you.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.950
You’ll just ignore me.”

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.270
His response was similar when asked when he
was born.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:44.510
He even claimed that Dr. Loyd wouldn’t notice
if he punched him in the nose.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:49.630
Dr. Loyd seemed undisturbed, acting as if
he had just been told a year instead of being

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:50.630
threatened.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:53.910
Then SCP-1504 decided to test his theory.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:58.410
The mysterious “Joe Schmo” leaped up from
his seat and punched Dr. Loyd.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:03.350
The doctor’s nose began bleeding badly,
but he seemed to hardly notice, only commenting

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.260
that he had a nosebleed and leaving to take
care of it.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:12.450
This made SCP-1504 even more agitated, cursing
at Dr. Loyd and desperately seeking to get

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.450
his attention.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:19.780
As Dr. Loyd asked why he couldn’t seem to
be hurt, SCP-1509 lost his head.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.930
He began an extended rant where he stated
that he could do anything to anyone, even

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.180
kill the people they love, and they wouldn’t
notice.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:33.200
He claimed to be able to shoot himself with
the guard’s gun, and nothing would happen.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.510
SCP-1504 was in tears, but no one seemed to
notice.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:43.280
Dr. Loyd just kept writing notes as SCP-1504
ranted that he always felt like he was stuck

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.090
in a room crowded with people, and every single
one of them ignored him.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.550
He expressed that he wished to die, but was
apparently unable to due to the nature of

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:53.580
his anomaly.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:59.340
Dr. Loyd didn’t seem to hear any of this,
and instead thanked SCP-1504 for cooperating

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.140
with the interview and returned him to his
cell.

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:06.740
His perception of the interview was exactly
what the initial interview had been - completely

00:06:06.740 --> 00:06:08.200
uneventful.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:14.990
It was clear that SCP-1504 was much more powerful
than anyone knew - and now he was missing.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:20.840
The Foundation met and quickly updated SCP-1504’s
classification from Safe to Keter.

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:25.900
The classification and description was pieced
together - slowly - due to the subject’s

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:31.050
cognitohazard abilities, which means that
any information known about him may be subjective

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.050
at any time.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:37.710
A place for him was prepared at Area 114,
the Foundation’s primary location for containing

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:40.460
perception and sensory-based threats.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:47.900
But SCP-1504 is not currently contained - and
his unique abilities mean he may never be.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:53.420
After all, how do you contain something when
no one knows who or where it is?

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.371
But the Foundation is prepared.

00:06:55.371 --> 00:07:01.270
There’s a cell waiting for SCP-1504 at the
site, a simple-looking 3 meter by 3 meter

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:06.050
by 3 meter chamber, but the security on hand
is anything but simple.

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:11.210
It will be kept closely guarded, with a minimum
of four Level 3 staff members required for

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.210
access.

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:16.500
Two staff members will stay inside the control
room ready to trigger security measures and

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.860
even the failsafe if a containment breach
happens.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:23.930
The staff is ready to flood the cell with
Halothane gas if needed - one of the only

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:30.560
things that can incapacitate SCP-1504, along
with a sharp blow to the head.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:36.170
He cannot be allowed to escape, and must be
confined and restrained at all times.

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:40.570
Any attempt to open the locks must be released
by multiple staff members at the same time,

00:07:40.570 --> 00:07:46.050
and only one can enter the chamber to interact
with SCP-1504.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:50.300
So what do we know about what makes SCP-1504
so dangerous?

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.430
Well, that depends on who you ask.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:57.810
Because most people would say there’s absolutely
nothing dangerous or unique about him.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.050
He’s just an average Joe.

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:03.650
And that’s exactly what makes him so dangerous.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:09.840
SCP-1504 is a living cognitohazard that affects
the perception of everyone around him.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:15.260
No matter what he does, it will be perceived
as normal, calm, and forgettable - and the

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:20.770
odds are anyone around him will forget his
existence only seconds after they meet him.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:23.410
But that’s not his most dangerous ability.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:28.430
In addition to his cognitohazard and his seeming
complete inability to be harmed beyond brief

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:34.719
incapacitation, SCP-1504 has the ability to
interfere with electronic systems - which

00:08:34.719 --> 00:08:37.899
caused the catastrophic breach at his original
site.

00:08:37.899 --> 00:08:42.440
Any automatic systems around him will start
to glitch, and as such his private cell at

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:48.449
site Area 114 is locked only with simple locks
featuring combinations and keys.

00:08:48.449 --> 00:08:52.800
Testing on the range of his powers is ongoing,
and the site will take care to make sure a

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.180
total containment failure is never allowed
to happen again.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:01.010
While the Foundation intends to minimize direct
contact with him once captured, any personnel

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:05.829
at Area 114 will already be trained in how
to resist perception shifts.

00:09:05.829 --> 00:09:10.420
For any of this to work though, the Foundation
has to capture him first.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:12.480
And therein lies the problem.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:18.170
The Foundation was able to capture SCP-1504
the first time simply by reports of his inability

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:19.490
to be harmed.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.230
That seems to be the one thing about him anyone
can notice.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:28.829
Otherwise, no action he takes - even physically
attacking someone - will be memorable in any

00:09:28.829 --> 00:09:32.629
way, allowing him to slip away undetected.

00:09:32.629 --> 00:09:36.920
While physically, he is little threat to anyone,
there is reason to consider him a critical

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:38.829
danger to public safety.

00:09:38.829 --> 00:09:43.639
His ability to disrupt electronic systems
means he could be a security risk to any public

00:09:43.639 --> 00:09:48.670
facility - including banks, prisons, or even
nuclear power plants.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.809
And there is reason to believe he may be growing
more unstable.

00:09:52.809 --> 00:09:58.420
No one knows how old SCP-1504 is, or if he
has a normal lifespan.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:02.800
His inability to be harmed indicates he could
be anomalous in other ways, and even if he

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:07.920
ages normally, it’s clear the isolation
of his abilities are making him increasingly

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.060
angry.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:14.519
He seems to be getting more and more desperate
to be noticed by any means necessary - hence

00:10:14.519 --> 00:10:17.580
his assault of the unfortunate Dr. Loyd.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:21.610
And now he’s out there in the world, undetected
by anyone.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:26.320
Who knows how he’ll try to make himself
famous - or infamous - next?

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:31.690
The Foundation has made the capture of SCP-1504
one of their highest priorities, and once

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:35.740
they get him, they intend to make sure he’s
never free again.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:41.180
Now they just have to find him, and that’s
where many Foundation experts are stumped.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.939
How do you find something that is designed
to go unnoticed?

00:10:44.939 --> 00:10:49.000
Until they have an answer, their trackers
are on the search for reports of a normal-looking

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:55.119
caucasian man, just under six feet tall, with
a small birthmark on his right shoulder.

00:10:55.119 --> 00:10:56.610
That should narrow it down.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:02.439
For more on another unassuming man with unexpected
abilities, check out “SCP-343 - God”,

00:11:02.439 --> 00:11:07.889
or watch “SCP-507 - Reluctant Dimension
Hopper” for another SCP whose control of

00:11:07.889 --> 00:11:09.709
its abilities is lacking.

